[E-PARTIAL] Error: a partial function can't be used where a total one is expected
    ╭─[ reject/partial-row-variable.sw:11:52 ]
    │
 11 │ def printed: List Text := Pair.fst (IO.simulate [] cat)
    │                                                    ─┬─  
    │                                                     ╰─── this might not finish: its type says `Partial`
    │ 
    │ Note 1: a function whose type doesn't say `Partial` must finish; a row with abilities, `{… | e}`, is total because a handler can't run partial code, so a function taking it can't be given a partial one (a bare `{e}` may stand for a partial row)
    │ 
    │ Note 2: to accept partial functions, write `Partial` in the row: `{Partial | e}`
────╯
